WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
The Lucy Show.

00:07.000 --> 00:14.000
Starring Lucille Ball.

00:14.000 --> 00:21.000
Co-starring Gail Gordon.

00:21.000 --> 00:33.000
Brought to you by...

00:33.000 --> 00:53.000
Brought to you by...

00:53.000 --> 00:55.000
Mrs. Carmichael!

00:55.000 --> 00:59.000
Those boots were made for walking.

00:59.000 --> 01:01.000
Well, I'm having trouble with this typewriter.

01:01.000 --> 01:05.000
Well, you shouldn't have. It's a brand new electric typewriter. A child could run it.

01:05.000 --> 01:10.000
Well, I'll bet Tom Edison himself couldn't work this one. Couldn't I have my old typewriter back?

01:10.000 --> 01:14.000
No. You simply have got to learn how to run that electric typewriter.

01:14.000 --> 01:19.000
Well, couldn't I break in slowly, like maybe on a gas typewriter?

01:19.000 --> 01:22.000
This is no time to be facetious, Mrs. Carmichael.

01:22.000 --> 01:23.000
Well...

01:23.000 --> 01:25.000
Now, did you put the paper in properly?

01:25.000 --> 01:26.000
Of course.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.000
Did you get the keys properly?

01:27.000 --> 01:28.000
Yes, I did.

01:28.000 --> 01:30.000
Did you plug it in properly?

01:30.000 --> 01:34.000
Oh, plug it in!

01:34.000 --> 01:37.000
Oh, you must think I'm a perfect idiot.

01:37.000 --> 01:40.000
Nobody's perfect.

01:40.000 --> 01:44.000
But you'll do until the real thing comes along.

01:44.000 --> 01:48.000
Now, Mrs. Carmichael, this is an electric typewriter.

01:48.000 --> 01:49.000
Yes, sir.

01:49.000 --> 01:52.000
This is the plug for the electric typewriter.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.000
Yes, sir.

01:53.000 --> 01:57.000
And this is the outlet that supplies the electricity for the electric typewriter.

01:57.000 --> 02:00.000
Oh, Mr. Mooney, I don't... Now, please don't interrupt.

02:00.000 --> 02:03.000
Now, the typewriter will not work without electricity.

02:03.000 --> 02:04.000
We must plug it in.

02:04.000 --> 02:09.000
So... Mr. Mooney, I... Please don't interrupt.

02:09.000 --> 02:15.000
So, we plug this into that bus leg.

02:21.000 --> 02:23.000
That's what I tried to tell you.

02:23.000 --> 02:26.000
That outlet has a short circuit.

02:26.000 --> 02:32.000
Now, if you don't mind, Mr. Mooney,

02:32.000 --> 02:38.000
we plug this into that duct leg.

02:49.000 --> 02:53.000
See, Mr. Mooney, this machine is wonderful.

02:53.000 --> 02:56.000
You know, it practically types by itself.

02:56.000 --> 02:59.000
I'll bet someday they invent a typewriter that does type by itself.

02:59.000 --> 03:02.000
And then you wouldn't need me.

03:02.000 --> 03:06.000
May I live to see the day.

03:06.000 --> 03:09.000
Oh, I don't think that was a very nice thing for you to say.

03:09.000 --> 03:10.000
No, you don't.

03:10.000 --> 03:11.000
No, I don't.

03:11.000 --> 03:15.000
You know something? You're always finding fault with me.

03:15.000 --> 03:19.000
If I'm so incompetent, how come you picked me from the secretarial pool?

03:19.000 --> 03:24.000
Picked you? You were the only one left.

03:24.000 --> 03:26.000
You know, you're lucky you got me.

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
Good help is very hard to find these days.

03:28.000 --> 03:32.000
I know. I'm still looking.

03:32.000 --> 03:35.000
It'll be a lot easier for me to go out and get another job

03:35.000 --> 03:37.000
than for you to find another secretary.

03:37.000 --> 03:40.000
You'll get another job?

03:40.000 --> 03:42.000
Ha!

03:42.000 --> 03:44.000
I could get another job if I wanted to.

03:44.000 --> 03:50.000
Well, it would be very interesting to see just what kind of a job you think you're qualified for.

03:50.000 --> 03:53.000
Well, I'm qualified for a lot more than you ever give me credit for.

03:53.000 --> 03:55.000
And I'd like a chance to prove it. I'll tell you that.

03:55.000 --> 03:56.000
All right, good, good.

03:56.000 --> 04:00.000
Why don't we start by looking in the help-wanted section of the newspaper?

04:00.000 --> 04:02.000
That's a very good idea.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.000
Oh, here we are.

04:03.000 --> 04:05.000
Help-wanted, female.

04:05.000 --> 04:10.000
Excellent position open for unusually talented young lady.

04:10.000 --> 04:15.000
College graduate with a master's degree in psychology

04:15.000 --> 04:22.000
and a thorough background in calculus, trigonometry, and mathematical analysis.

04:22.000 --> 04:31.000
Must speak six languages and be expert at operating a digital computer.

04:31.000 --> 04:33.000
What's their phone number?

04:33.000 --> 04:36.000
You're going to apply for the job?

04:36.000 --> 04:39.000
No, I'm going to call them and tell them not to count on me.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.000
I don't think so.

04:41.000 --> 04:44.000
Oh, here's another job that you're not qualified for.

04:44.000 --> 04:48.000
Mr. Mooney, if you don't mind, I'd prefer to select my own new job.

04:48.000 --> 04:49.000
Well, I was just trying to help.

04:49.000 --> 04:52.000
Thank you, but I'd like to find it.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.000
Oh, here's one.

04:53.000 --> 04:57.000
It's an ad for an employment agency that specializes in unusual jobs.

04:57.000 --> 04:59.000
The Unique Employment Agency.

04:59.000 --> 05:01.000
We get odd positions for odd people.

05:01.000 --> 05:04.000
Oh, that's you, all right.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.000
Never mind. I'm going right down and see them.

05:06.000 --> 05:09.000
You'll never find a job for anyone as incompetent as you are.

05:09.000 --> 05:11.000
I am not incompetent.

05:11.000 --> 05:14.000
I know what I'm doing every minute, and don't you...

05:14.000 --> 05:17.000
Never mind. Never mind. I'll take care of it.

05:17.000 --> 05:18.000
Go. Go.

05:18.000 --> 05:21.000
All right.

05:21.000 --> 05:24.000
Knows what she's doing every minute.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.000
I...

05:25.000 --> 05:27.000
I...

05:27.000 --> 05:29.000
I...

05:29.000 --> 05:31.000
I...

05:35.000 --> 05:38.000
Before we talk about your employment problems,

05:38.000 --> 05:40.000
I have some background information I'd like to ask you.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.000
Yes, ma'am.

05:42.000 --> 05:43.000
Name?

05:43.000 --> 05:45.000
Lucille Carmichael.

05:45.000 --> 05:46.000
Address?

05:46.000 --> 05:50.000
The Glen Hall apartment, 780 North Gower Street.

05:50.000 --> 05:52.000
Age?

05:52.000 --> 05:57.000
Would you mind putting down over 21?

05:57.000 --> 05:59.000
Over 21.

05:59.000 --> 06:02.000
Way over.

06:02.000 --> 06:04.000
Education?

06:04.000 --> 06:06.000
Yes, I'm a high school graduate,

06:06.000 --> 06:10.000
and I have two years of business college.

06:10.000 --> 06:11.000
Almost.

06:11.000 --> 06:14.000
Perhaps we should give you an aptitude test

06:14.000 --> 06:16.000
to find out the type of work for which you're qualified.

06:16.000 --> 06:17.000
All right.

06:17.000 --> 06:20.000
Now, this will be a word association test.

06:20.000 --> 06:23.000
I'll mention a word, and then you say whatever word pops into your head.

06:23.000 --> 06:24.000
Mm-hmm.

06:24.000 --> 06:25.000
Summer?

06:25.000 --> 06:26.000
Winter.

06:26.000 --> 06:27.000
Hot?

06:27.000 --> 06:28.000
Cold.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.000
Legs?

06:29.000 --> 06:30.000
Walk?

06:30.000 --> 06:31.000
Hair?

06:31.000 --> 06:33.000
Dye.

06:33.000 --> 06:37.000
I just used a little Hannah.

06:37.000 --> 06:38.000
Lift?

06:38.000 --> 06:39.000
Carry?

06:39.000 --> 06:41.000
Grant.

06:41.000 --> 06:42.000
Carry?

06:42.000 --> 06:43.000
Grant?

06:43.000 --> 06:45.000
Yes.

06:45.000 --> 06:49.000
What type of job would an answer like that qualify you for?

06:49.000 --> 06:52.000
I don't know, but it's nice work if you can get it.

06:52.000 --> 06:56.000
Well, I've had all kinds of answers from applicants, but carry?

06:56.000 --> 06:57.000
Grant?

06:57.000 --> 06:59.000
Yeah, well, I wouldn't mind working for him in any capacity.

06:59.000 --> 07:03.000
And you know, these days he could use a babysitter.

07:03.000 --> 07:06.000
Say, would you like to do some babysitting?

07:06.000 --> 07:07.000
Oh, I sure would.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.000
Does carry grant need a babysitter?

07:09.000 --> 07:10.000
No, no, no, no.

07:10.000 --> 07:11.000
This is a wonderful babysitting job.

07:11.000 --> 07:13.000
I don't know why I didn't think of it before.

07:13.000 --> 07:15.000
Oh, now, there are three children,

07:15.000 --> 07:18.000
and it pays $5 per hour per child,

07:18.000 --> 07:21.000
with a guarantee of three hours.

07:21.000 --> 07:23.000
Oh, wow, that's $45.

07:23.000 --> 07:25.000
I'll take it.

07:25.000 --> 07:27.000
Well, you can have it if you qualify.

07:27.000 --> 07:30.000
Oh, well, I raised two children of my own.

07:30.000 --> 07:31.000
They're away at school now.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.000
Oh, well, then you know all about the care of babies.

07:34.000 --> 07:35.000
Oh, I certainly do.

07:35.000 --> 07:39.000
I always followed a simple poem that my mother taught me.

07:39.000 --> 07:43.000
If you want a happy baby, here's the thing to try.

07:43.000 --> 07:46.000
Keep one end fed and the other end dry.

07:46.000 --> 07:50.000
Oh, that's very good child psychology.

07:50.000 --> 07:52.000
Oh, you'll do just fine for this job.

07:52.000 --> 07:53.000
Thank you.

07:53.000 --> 07:55.000
Now, the family name is Winslow,

07:55.000 --> 07:58.000
and it's at 1711 Valley Meadow Road.

07:58.000 --> 08:00.000
You'll be there at 7 o'clock tonight.

08:00.000 --> 08:02.000
Yes, ma'am, I will, and thank you very much.

08:02.000 --> 08:04.000
You're welcome.

08:13.000 --> 08:14.000
Hello, Mrs. Winslow.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.000
This is Miss Allman.

08:16.000 --> 08:18.000
Oh, I have good news for you.

08:18.000 --> 08:22.000
There'll be a babysitter there tonight at 7 o'clock.

08:22.000 --> 08:25.000
No, I didn't tell her about the children.

08:25.000 --> 08:28.000
I was afraid if I did, she wouldn't take the job.

08:31.000 --> 08:34.000
Darling, what time is the babysitter going to get here?

08:34.000 --> 08:36.000
I told you before, 7 o'clock.

08:36.000 --> 08:40.000
I hope this one stays long enough for us to get out of the house.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.000
Yes, dear.

08:41.000 --> 08:45.000
Darling, why don't we ever hire an animal trainer instead of a babysitter?

08:45.000 --> 08:46.000
An animal trainer?

08:46.000 --> 08:47.000
Yes, dear.

08:47.000 --> 08:52.000
After all, they are chimpanzees, and chimpanzees are animals.

08:52.000 --> 08:54.000
They're just as human as you are.

08:54.000 --> 08:56.000
Yes, dear.

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
Oh, that must be the babysitter. I'll get it.

08:58.000 --> 08:59.000
I'll get it.

08:59.000 --> 09:01.000
You round up the children.

09:01.000 --> 09:02.000
Yes, dear.

09:07.000 --> 09:08.000
Welcome in.

09:08.000 --> 09:11.000
Thank you.

09:13.000 --> 09:16.000
Oh, my, what a lovely room.

09:16.000 --> 09:18.000
Well, it's a little messy just now.

09:18.000 --> 09:20.000
The children have been playing in here all day.

09:20.000 --> 09:21.000
I understand.

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
They certainly have a lot of nice toys.

09:23.000 --> 09:25.000
Oh, and that wonderful tree.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.000
Children love to climb trees.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.000
Especially ours.

09:29.000 --> 09:31.000
They can climb more than they can walk.

09:32.000 --> 09:35.000
They sound like very unusual children.

09:35.000 --> 09:37.000
Yes, they are.

09:37.000 --> 09:38.000
And their names.

09:38.000 --> 09:41.000
Their names are Danny, Charlie, and Bobby.

09:41.000 --> 09:43.000
Oh, how wonderful. Three boys.

09:43.000 --> 09:45.000
No, no, no, no. Bobby is short for Roberta.

09:45.000 --> 09:47.000
Oh, Roberta is the baby.

09:47.000 --> 09:49.000
Now, she'll require a little extra attention, of course.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.000
Naturally.

09:50.000 --> 09:52.000
Now, she has to be in bed by 7.30.

09:52.000 --> 09:53.000
She sleeps here in the crib.

09:53.000 --> 09:55.000
That's her nightgown.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.000
The milk and the cereal over here.

09:57.000 --> 10:00.000
The boys sleep back here in these bunk beds.

10:00.000 --> 10:01.000
Bunk beds are wonderful.

10:01.000 --> 10:04.000
Yes, and these are their pajamas.

10:04.000 --> 10:07.000
Aren't the sleeves a little long?

10:08.000 --> 10:10.000
No, not for them.

10:11.000 --> 10:14.000
She likes to be rocked and sung to at bedtime.

10:14.000 --> 10:16.000
Do you know any lullabies?

10:16.000 --> 10:17.000
Yes.

10:17.000 --> 10:20.000
Does she like Rock-A-Bye Baby and the Tree Top?

10:20.000 --> 10:22.000
Oh, she loves the part about the tree top.

10:23.000 --> 10:25.000
In fact, she likes all kinds of music.

10:25.000 --> 10:28.000
She likes rock and roll, Dixieland, boogie-woogie.

10:28.000 --> 10:32.000
Well, for a baby, she sounds like a real swinger.

10:32.000 --> 10:34.000
They're all swingers.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.000
Oh, that's why we have the tree.

10:38.000 --> 10:40.000
I can hardly wait to meet the little darling.

10:40.000 --> 11:06.000
Oh, here they come now.

11:06.000 --> 11:08.000
Aren't they cute?

11:08.000 --> 11:11.000
Well, yes, they're cute, all right.

11:11.000 --> 11:14.000
Aren't they a little unusual looking?

11:14.000 --> 11:16.000
Yes, they're monkeys.

11:16.000 --> 11:18.000
You said that, I didn't.

11:18.000 --> 11:22.000
Oh, that's why this babysitting job pays so well, huh?

11:22.000 --> 11:23.000
Yes.

11:23.000 --> 11:24.000
You're not going to back out, are you?

11:24.000 --> 11:28.000
Uh, no, I can use the money.

11:28.000 --> 11:29.000
Good.

11:29.000 --> 11:30.000
Well, let's get going, Jonathan.

11:30.000 --> 11:31.000
Yes, dear.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.000
Here, Mrs. Carver-Montague.

11:32.000 --> 11:33.000
Come on, don't be a good boy.

11:33.000 --> 11:34.000
Come along.

11:34.000 --> 11:35.000
We'll be back right after the movie.

11:35.000 --> 11:36.000
Come on.

11:36.000 --> 11:37.000
Come on.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.000
Hello, Bobby.

11:47.000 --> 11:48.000
Hello.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.000
Hey, you.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.000
Charlie.

11:52.000 --> 11:53.000
Danny.

11:53.000 --> 11:54.000
Come here, Danny.

11:56.000 --> 11:57.000
Hello there, fellas.

11:58.000 --> 11:59.000
There.

11:59.000 --> 12:00.000
Hey.

12:00.000 --> 12:01.000
Hey there, fellas.

12:01.000 --> 12:02.000
What is it?

12:05.000 --> 12:12.000
So rosy, pockets all are cozy, up or down, up or down.

12:13.000 --> 12:15.000
All right, all right, now, wait a minute, wait a minute.

12:15.000 --> 12:17.000
Wait a minute, now, boys, stop it.

12:17.000 --> 12:19.000
Danny, sit up there on the chair.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.000
Sit up there on the chair.

12:21.000 --> 12:22.000
Now, you hold the baby for me.

12:22.000 --> 12:23.000
Come on.

12:23.000 --> 12:24.000
I'll ride the horsey with you, Charlie.

12:24.000 --> 12:25.000
Get on the horsey.

12:25.000 --> 12:27.000
Hold the baby now, Danny.

12:27.000 --> 12:28.000
Danny, hold the baby.

12:28.000 --> 12:29.000
Do you hear me?

12:29.000 --> 12:31.000
Hold on to the baby.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.000
Wait a minute, now.

12:43.000 --> 12:45.000
All right, Charlie, you'll beat me this time.

12:46.000 --> 12:47.000
Okay, okay.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.000
Get up on the bunks, Charlie, and play.

12:49.000 --> 12:51.000
Danny, come on, get up on the bunks here.

12:52.000 --> 12:53.000
I'll take the baby.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.000
Get up on the bunks and play.

12:54.000 --> 12:55.000
Come here, Charlie.

12:55.000 --> 12:56.000
Come on, get up here.

12:56.000 --> 12:57.000
Lay up on top, Charlie.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.000
Lay up on top.

12:59.000 --> 13:00.000
Now, get up there and play.

13:01.000 --> 13:02.000
I've just got to get the baby to bed.

13:03.000 --> 13:04.000
Come here, Bobby.

13:05.000 --> 13:06.000
Come on, sweetheart.

13:07.000 --> 13:08.000
Oh, Danny.

13:08.000 --> 13:09.000
Danny, come on, back.

13:09.000 --> 13:10.000
Danny, come on, get over in the bunks.

13:11.000 --> 13:12.000
Please.

13:12.000 --> 13:13.000
Let me get the baby to bed.

13:15.000 --> 13:16.000
Oh, good heavens.

13:17.000 --> 13:20.000
Now, stay there and play by yourselves, do you hear?

13:21.000 --> 13:22.000
Oh.

13:23.000 --> 13:24.000
Oh, boy, those brothers of yours.

13:24.000 --> 13:26.000
Oh, good heavens, hang on.

13:30.000 --> 13:31.000
Off we go and into our nightie.

13:32.000 --> 13:33.000
Come on, darling.

13:34.000 --> 13:35.000
Come on, sweetheart.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.000
Oh, that's a good baby.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.000
Put your arm in there.

13:41.000 --> 13:42.000
Oh, dear.

13:44.000 --> 13:45.000
Oh, I'm exhausted.

13:46.000 --> 13:47.000
I don't know about you.

13:48.000 --> 13:49.000
I'm ready to go to bed.

13:51.000 --> 13:52.000
They haven't even had your dinner yet.

13:52.000 --> 13:53.000
They haven't even had your din-din yet.

13:54.000 --> 13:55.000
You ready for your bottle?

13:56.000 --> 13:57.000
Oh, turn around, honey.

13:58.000 --> 13:59.000
That's it.

14:00.000 --> 14:01.000
I've got a facet here.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.000
Put your head up.

14:04.000 --> 14:05.000
That's a good baby.

14:06.000 --> 14:07.000
That's a good baby.

14:08.000 --> 14:09.000
We're getting tired, isn't it?

14:10.000 --> 14:11.000
Those brothers are so crazy.

14:12.000 --> 14:13.000
Come on, sweetheart.

14:16.000 --> 14:17.000
Now, how about our bottle, huh?

14:18.000 --> 14:19.000
How about our bottle?

14:19.000 --> 14:21.000
Now, wait a minute, darling.

14:22.000 --> 14:23.000
Now, don't just take it easy.

14:24.000 --> 14:25.000
Take it easy.

14:26.000 --> 14:27.000
We're going to sit down, we're going to walk,

14:28.000 --> 14:29.000
and we're going to have our bottle.

14:30.000 --> 14:31.000
Okay.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.000
Oh.

14:34.000 --> 14:35.000
Oh.

14:41.000 --> 14:44.000
Are you supposed to ride a bicycle in the house?

14:45.000 --> 14:46.000
Are you supposed to ride a bicycle in the house?

14:46.000 --> 14:48.000
Oh, darling, honey, I'm sure.

14:53.000 --> 14:54.000
Come here.

14:55.000 --> 14:56.000
Come here, darling, honey.

14:57.000 --> 14:58.000
Darling, darling.

14:59.000 --> 15:00.000
Oh, boy, honestly.

15:01.000 --> 15:02.000
Darling, come here.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.000
Oh, boy, please.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.000
Stick that in your mouth.

15:07.000 --> 15:10.000
Now, boy, you mustn't fight like this.

15:11.000 --> 15:12.000
Danny, sit up here in the chair.

15:13.000 --> 15:14.000
Yes, darling, leave him alone.

15:14.000 --> 15:15.000
Oh, honestly.

15:16.000 --> 15:17.000
You can sit.

15:18.000 --> 15:19.000
Darling, darling.

15:20.000 --> 15:21.000
Danny, get up here in the chair.

15:22.000 --> 15:23.000
Yes, let go of Charlie.

15:24.000 --> 15:25.000
Oh, boy.

15:26.000 --> 15:27.000
Danny, will you get up there?

15:28.000 --> 15:29.000
Darling, stay, honey.

15:30.000 --> 15:31.000
Darling.

15:33.000 --> 15:34.000
Listen, you.

15:35.000 --> 15:36.000
Get up there.

15:37.000 --> 15:38.000
Charlie, get up there with your hat.

15:39.000 --> 15:40.000
Get up there at the table.

15:41.000 --> 15:42.000
Get up there at the table.

15:42.000 --> 15:43.000
Get up there in your chair.

15:44.000 --> 15:45.000
Sit right down there.

15:46.000 --> 15:47.000
Oh, Danny.

15:48.000 --> 15:49.000
Come over here.

15:50.000 --> 15:51.000
Get up there in your chair.

15:52.000 --> 15:53.000
